Maintainer: Thomas Winkler <thomas.winkler@iggmp.net>
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Standards-Version: 4.7.0

Package: cinema-player
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-tk, mpv, ffmpeg, x11-xserver-utils, xfonts-utils, edid-decode
Recommends: mutter-common-bin, kscreen
Description: cinema video player for a projector booth
 Cinema Player runs two mpv instances: one on the projector and one in the
 booth window. The playlist holds films and stills. The projector picture
 stays free of menus and on-screen text.
 .
 On X11 the projector mode is set with xrandr. GNOME on Wayland uses gdctl
 (mutter-common-bin). KDE on Wayland uses kscreen-doctor (kscreen).
 DMX over a USB interface needs the user in the dialout group.
